- `Rc<RefCell<T>>`: single-threaded shared ownership. `Rc` counts references; `RefCell` gives runtime-checked mutable access. Not `Send`/`Sync`. Use when data is shared within one thread.
- `Arc<Mutex<T>>`: thread-safe shared ownership. `Arc` uses atomic reference counting; `Mutex` provides exclusive locking. Use across threads.

```rust
use std::rc::Rc;
use std::cell::RefCell;

let shared = Rc::new(RefCell::new(String::from("hello")));
let clone = shared.clone();
clone.borrow_mut().push_str("!"); // runtime borrow check
```

```rust
use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};

let shared = Arc::new(Mutex::new(String::from("hello")));
let clone = shared.clone();
clone.lock().unwrap().push_str("!"); // exclusive lock
```

Rule of thumb: `Rc<RefCell<T>>` for single-threaded shared mutable state; `Arc<Mutex<T>>` for multi-threaded shared mutable state.

